          "model_output": "To find the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ such that $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 2$ and $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix},$ we can use the dot product and cross product of vectors.\n\nThe dot product of two vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\end{vmatrix} = a_1b_1 + a_2b_2 + a_3b_3\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$\n\nThe dot product of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = 1 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot -1 + 1 \\cdot 1 = -1 + 2 + 1 = -3\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ such that $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = -3$ and $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$\n\nThe cross product of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\end{vmatrix} \\begin{vmatrix} b_1 & b_2 & b_3 \\end{vmatrix} = a_1b_2 - a_2b_1 + a_3b_3\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$\n\nThe cross product of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} \\begin{vmatrix} 2 & -1 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = 1 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 1 = -1 - 2 + 1 = -3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ such that $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = -3$ and $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ is $\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}}.$",
