          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the maximum number of pencils that Zach can place into each of the three bags while maintaining the same number of pencils in each bag.\n\n1. **Understanding the Problem:**\n   - Zach has three bags and a bunch of pencils to be placed into the bags.\n   - He is told to place the greatest number of pencils possible into each of the three bags while also keeping the number of pencils in each bag the same.\n\n2. **Finding the Maximum Number of Pencils:**\n   - The maximum number of pencils that can be placed into each bag is the total number of pencils minus the number of pencils already placed in the bags.\n   - Since the number of pencils in each bag is the same, the maximum number of pencils is the total number of pencils minus the number of pencils already placed in the bags.\n\n3. **Calculating the Maximum Number of Pencils:**\n   - The total number of pencils is 3.\n   - The number of pencils already placed in the bags is 2.\n   - The maximum number of pencils that can be placed into each bag is the total number of pencils minus the number of pencils already placed in the bags.\n   - The maximum number of pencils that can be placed into each bag is 3 - 2 = 1.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The greatest number of pencils that Zach could have left over is 1.\n\nTherefore, the answer is $\\boxed{1}$.",
