(\\frac{1}{b}-a\\right)$ and then finding the greatest possible value of $\\frac{a+1}{b}\\left(\\frac{1}{b}-a\\right)$.\n\nThe greatest possible value of $\\frac{a+1}{b}\\left(\\frac{1}{b}-a\\right)$ is $\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{2}}$.\n\nThis problem tests the understanding of the relationship between the product of two fractions and the product of their reciprocals, as well as the ability to find the greatest possible value of a product of two fractions.",
