          "unique_id": "test/algebra/1282.json",
          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we start by recognizing that $\\sqrt{120-\\sqrt{x}}$ is an integer if and only if $120-\\sqrt{x}$ is an integer. This is because $\\sqrt{120-\\sqrt{x}}$ is the square root of the difference between $120$ and $\\sqrt{x}$, which is an integer.\n\nNext, we use the fact that $\\sqrt{x}$ is an integer if and only if $x$ is a perfect square. This is because $\\sqrt{x}$ is the square root of $x$, and a perfect square is an integer.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the problem is $\\boxed{x$ is a perfect square}$",
