          "model_output": "To solve the given problem, we start by simplifying the given expression:\n\n$$\\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r-7} = 4r-3.$$\n\nFirst, we simplify the numerator:\n\n$$6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 6r^2 - 19r - 7 + 7 = 6r^2 - 19r + 7.$$\n\nNext, we simplify the denominator:\n\n$$2r-7 = 2r - 7 + 7 = 2r - 7 + 7 = 2r + 4.$$\n\nNow, we substitute the simplified expressions back into the original expression:\n\n$$\\frac{6r^2 - 19r + 7}{2r + 4} = 4r - 3.$$\n\nTo solve for $r$, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2r + 4$:\n\n$$2r + 4 \\cdot 4r - 3 = 2r + 4 \\cdot 4r - 3.$$\n\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\n$$8r - 12 = 8r - 12.$$\n\nNow, we subtract $8r - 12$ from both sides:\n\n$$8r - 12 - 8r - 12 = 8r - 12 - 8r - 12.$$\n\n$$8r - 20 = 0.$$\n\nSolving for $r$, we get:\n\n$$r = \\frac{20}{8} = \\frac{5}{2}.$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $r$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{5}{2}}$.",
