          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of points in the interior of the rectangular region.\n\n1. **Identify the vertices:**\n   - The vertices of the rectangular region are $(5,4), (-5,4), (-5,-4), (5,-4)$.\n\n2. **Determine the interior points:**\n   - The interior points of the rectangular region are the points that are not on the boundary of the region.\n   - The interior points are the points that are not on the line $x=4$ or $x=-4$.\n\n3. **Count interior points:**\n   - The interior points are the points that are not on the line $x=4$ or $x=-4$.\n   - The interior points are the points that are not on the line $x=5$ or $x=-5$.\n\n4. **Calculate the number of interior points:**\n   - The number of interior points is the number of points that are not on the line $x=5$ or $x=-5$.\n   - The number of interior points is the number of points that are not on the line $x=4$ or $x=-4$.\n\n5. **Sum the interior points:**\n   - The sum of the interior points is the number of interior points plus the number of points that are on the line $x=4$ or $x=-4$.\n   - The sum of the interior points is the number of interior points plus the number of points that are on the line $x=5$ or $x=-5$.\n\n6. **Calculate the sum:**\n   - The sum of the interior points is $5+4+4+4=17$.\n\n7. **Conclusion:**\n   - The number of points with integer coordinates that will be strictly in the interior of the rectangular region is $\\boxed{17}$.",
