          "unique_id": "test/algebra/1936.json",
          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to find the value of $b$ such that $f(q(1)) = -3$.\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x)$:\n$$f'(x) = \\frac{d}{dx}(x - 3) = 1 - 3x = -2x.$$\nNext, we find the derivative of $q(x)$:\n$$q'(x) = bx + 1 = b \\cdot 1 + 1 = b.$$\nSubstituting these values into the equation $f(q(1)) = -3$, we get:\n$$(-2x)(-1) = -3.$$\nSimplifying, we have:\n$$-2x = -3.$$\nDividing both sides by -2, we get:\n$$x = 3.$$\nTherefore, the value of $b$ is $\\boxed{3}$.",
