          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to consider two configurations: one where all 8 people are seated around the table, and another where 2 people are seated on each side of the table.\n\n1. **Seating Configuration 1:**\n   - All 8 people are seated around the table.\n   - This configuration is equivalent to seating 8 people around a circle.\n   - The number of ways to seat 8 people around a circle is $\\binom{8}{2} = \\boxed{56}$.\n\n2. **Seating Configuration 2:**\n   - 2 people are seated on each side of the table.\n   - This configuration is equivalent to seating 2 people on each side of a square.\n   - The number of ways to seat 2 people on each side of a square is $\\binom{2}{1} \\cdot \\binom{2}{1} = \\boxed{4}$.\n\nConclusion:\nThe number of ways to seat 8 people around a square table with 2 people on each side is $\\boxed{56}$ and $\\boxed{4}$.",
