          "model_output": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the probability that a point chosen from the interior of the rectangle $ABCD$ is closer to $O$ than to any of the four vertices.\n\n1. **Define the coordinates of the vertices:**\n   - Let $O$ be the center of the rectangle.\n   - Let $A$ be the point with coordinates $(x_1, y_1)$ and $B$ be the point with coordinates $(x_2, y_2)$.\n   - Let $C$ be the point with coordinates $(x_3, y_3)$ and $D$ be the point with coordinates $(x_4, y_4)$.\n\n2. **Calculate the distance from $O$ to each vertex:**\n   - The distance from $O$ to $A$ is $x_1 - x_2 = x_1 - x_3 = x_1 - x_4 = k$.\n   - The distance from $O$ to $B$ is $y_1 - y_2 = y_1 - y_3 = y_1 - y_4 = k$.\n   - The distance from $O$ to $C$ is $x_2 - x_3 = x_2 - x_4 = x_2 - x_1 = k$.\n   - The distance from $O$ to $D$ is $y_2 - y_3 = y_2 - y_4 = y_2 - y_1 = k$.\n\n3. **Calculate the probability of being closer to $O$ than to any of the vertices:**\n   - The probability of being closer to $O$ than $A$ is $P(O < A) = \\frac{k}{x_1 - x_2} = \\frac{k}{k} = 1$.\n   - The probability of being closer to $O$ than $B$ is $P(O < B) = \\frac{k}{y_1 - y_2} = \\frac{k}{k} = 1$.\n   - The probability of being closer to $O$ than $C$ is $P(O < C) = \\frac{k}{x_2 - x_3} = \\frac{k}{k} = 1$.\n   - The probability of being closer to $O$ than $D$ is $P(O < D) = \\frac{k}{y_2 - y_3} = \\frac{k}{k} = 1$.\n\n4. **Calculate the total probability:**\n   - The total probability of being closer to $O$ than $A$ is $P(O < A) + P(O < B) + P(O < C) + P(O < D) = \\frac{k}{x_1 - x_2} + \\frac{k}{y_1 - y_2} + \\frac{k}{x_2 - x_3} + \\frac{k}{y_2 - y_3} = \\frac{k}{k} + \\frac{k}{k} + \\frac{k}{k} + \\frac{k}{k} = \\frac{2k}{k} = 2$.\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - The probability that a point chosen from the interior of the rectangle $ABCD$ is closer to $O$ than to any of the vertices is $\\boxed{2}$.",
